segler (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The macOS bundle says Segler is offered in German. The German itself
    shipped in 0.1.1, but the property list never claimed it, so App Store
    Connect listed English alone and the per-app language picker had nothing
    for a German speaker to choose. No change for a Debian user.
  * The property list parses. Two of its comments wrote out a command's flag
    with a double hyphen in it, which is illegal inside an XML comment.
  * The application icon is a full-bleed square rather than a boat in a blue
    roundel, because every store frames an icon in a square and rounds the
    corners itself. The two document icons keep the page shape.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:16:22 -0500

segler (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Selecting a heading no longer changes it. A heading whose level the element
    pane could not show — the document spelling it as zero, or deeper than the
    field's range — was rewritten to the nearest level the field could show the
    moment the heading was selected, marking the document modified, and a save
    would have written that substitution to the file. Selecting an element is
    not an edit. The field's range is the schema's now, so a level the
    specification allows is shown as itself.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 19:05:11 -0500

segler (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * German. Segler comes up in German on a machine set to German — the
    toolbar, both panes, the dialogs and the status line — reading the
    language the desktop already knows, with nothing to choose and English
    for any other. What the document says stays as the document says it: an
    element's name, an attribute's name and the values you pick from a list
    are the file's own words and are never translated.
  * The first release carrying an arm64 package.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 18:13:00 -0500

segler (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First packaged build. A window whose main pane is the document rendered
    from the tree and edited in place, with the element tree on the left, the
    element's properties on the right, and an archive's page images as an
    optional side panel. Validation against the DocLang schema and rules, with
    each finding a click from its element. The segler command-line tool over
    the same library: inspect, validate, page, render, table, edit and corpus.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 14:40:19 -0500
